<title>GERMANY: W.German Jan industry output falls 0.5 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>W.German Jan industry output falls 0.5 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Jan 97     Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -0.5	 +0.3	 +0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.2	 +2.0	  n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		95.5	 96.0	 94.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. @ The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Jan 97		  Dec 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     86.9	 -3.7     90.2	 +4.9</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   96.0	 +1.4     94.7	 -0.5</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   96.7	 -2.8     99.5	 +0.6</p>
<p>	Capital goods    102.3	 +8.6     94.2	 -1.7</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 84.3	 +3.8     81.2	 -2.6</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    89.8	 -1.3     91.0	 -0.5</p>
<p> Energy output	   110.9	 +0.1    110.8	 +3.0</p>
<p> Construction	     79.9	-21.3    101.5	 +7.9 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Dec 96/Jan 97 with Oct/Nov 96:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    +0.5 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Dec 96/Jan 97 with Dec 95/Jan 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +1.4</p>
<p> Mining				    +1.1</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +1.8</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     +2.1</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +2.7</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	+0.5</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -0.2</p>
<p> Energy output			   +2.9</p>
<p> Construction			    -4.7</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
